# Build context for ./frontend builds (compose + CI: context ./frontend).
# This file is load-bearing: the Dockerfile does `COPY . .` AFTER
# `npm ci`, so without it the host's node_modules (wrong platform
# binaries) would overwrite the image's fresh install, a stale dist/
# would ride along, and .env* would land in the build context — the
# image's VITE_* values come from the ARGs compose and CI pass, not
# from a copied file. The root .dockerignore does not apply: Docker
# only reads .dockerignore from the root of the build context.
.env
.env.*
node_modules
dist
dist-e2e
test-results
.git
.github
